{
 "_doc": "Stream B (play-test 2, Q10). Every townsperson who sells or serves gets their OWN building in the town plan. tools/bake-zone.mjs hands `byKind[<settlement kind>]` to proctown's opt-in `trades` option (planTown({trades:{list, share, pick:'square'}})): each entry is one plot, in priority order, nearest the square first, never shared; what does not fit falls off the end. The building placement then carries data.office (the want), data.role (the NPC role that works there, from `roles`), data.lit (true = a shop/service that should look open and lit to draw players in; false = an office you go to on purpose: no shop lights) and data.label (the sign text a client may draw). A role with no plot in a small settlement falls back the usual way (E's schedules.json anchors). Wants new to proctown here: shop, temple, barber, counting_house, study, armoury, bowyer, tailor, apothecary, provisioner, jeweller (proctown/data/cultures.json wantBases has shapes for them). Change this file -> re-bake the zones (tools/bake-zone.mjs --province torbor_downs).",
